5. Grid BFS

In a grid: Each cell is a node.

Example: 
0 0 0
0 1 0
0 0 0

A cell has up to 4 neighbours:

       UP
        ↑
LEFT ← cell → RIGHT
        ↓
      DOWN

Use:

int[] dr = {-1, 1, 0, 0};
int[] dc = {0, 0, -1, 1};
Basic Grid BFS

Code:

void bfs(int[][] grid, int sr, int sc) {

    int n = grid.length;
    int m = grid[0].length;

    boolean[][] visited = new boolean[n][m];
    Queue<int[]> q = new LinkedList<>();

    q.add(new int[]{sr, sc});
    visited[sr][sc] = true;

    int[] dr = {-1, 1, 0, 0};
    int[] dc = {0, 0, -1, 1};

    while(!q.isEmpty()) {
        int[] cell = q.poll();
        int r = cell[0];
        int c = cell[1];
        for(int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            int nr = r + dr[i];
            int nc = c + dc[i];
            // Outside grid
            if(nr < 0 || nr >= n ||
               nc < 0 || nc >= m) {
                continue;
            }

            // Already visited
            if(visited[nr][nc]) {
                continue;
            }

            visited[nr][nc] = true;
            q.add(new int[]{nr, nc});
        }
    }

nr , nc - new row new coloumn
We're asking: "If I move from the current cell in one of the 4 directions, what cell will I reach?"
}
